    pr_ref:  # c155
    description: "Found by the 2026-10-20 docstring-staleness audit (verifier reproduced). starlark.py ~L275 stores only `ctx.load_aliases[alias] = source_file` and drops the original name; ~L423-430 looks up `original_name = target_name`, i.e. the alias (`cr` for `load(\"//x:defs.bzl\", cr = \"custom_rule\")`). That is never a registered symbol name, so `cr(...)` resolves to `starlark:external:cr:function` instead of the loaded `custom_rule`. The module docstring and `_extract_starlark_edges` docstring both claim load aliases are used as path hints for cross-file resolution. Fix: keep (label, original_name) per alias, look up the original name, normalise the label to a path fragment for the hint. Docstring left stating the intent."  # c155
    fields: {}  # c155
